<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">cooldowns</ansi>

Cooldowns prevent spamming powerful abilities by enforcing waiting periods between uses.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What Are Cooldowns? ━━━</ansi>

Some abilities are powerful enough that they can't be used every round. After using
such an ability, it enters a cooldown period measured in combat rounds. You must wait
for the cooldown to expire before using that ability again.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Special Combat Move Cooldowns ━━━</ansi>

The special combat moves (<ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>) share a single cooldown:

  <ansi fg="stat">Shared Cooldown:</ansi> 5 rounds
  Using any special move triggers the cooldown for all three moves.

  <ansi fg="red">Example:</ansi>
  - Round 1: You use <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi> (starts 5-round cooldown)
  - Round 2-6: Cannot use bash, trip, or kick (cooldown active)
  - Round 7: Special moves available again

This prevents chaining knockdown attempts and encourages tactical timing.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Viewing Your Cooldowns ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cooldowns</ansi>
  Display all active cooldowns and remaining rounds

The command shows which abilities are on cooldown and how many rounds remain before
each becomes available again.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Abilities with Cooldowns ━━━</ansi>

Currently cooldowns apply to:
  - <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi> - Shield bash (5-round shared cooldown)
  - <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi> - Leg sweep (5-round shared cooldown)
  - <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi> - Power kick (5-round shared cooldown)

More abilities with cooldowns may be added in the future.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Cooldown Mechanics ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Round-Based:</ansi> Cooldowns tick down once per combat round
  <ansi fg="stat">Combat Only:</ansi> Cooldowns only matter during active combat
  <ansi fg="stat">Shared Cooldowns:</ansi> Some abilities share cooldown timers
  <ansi fg="stat">Prevented Actions:</ansi> Attempting to use a cooldown ability shows remaining time

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

